1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,518
This candle is green. But did buyers really win inside it?

2
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:16,160
A candle tells us only four things: open, high, low and close.

3
00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:23,036
But what happened inside, who bought how much and who sold how much, stays hidden.

4
00:00:23,485 --> 00:00:29,207
Now look inside. At the top levels, sellers sold far more than buyers bought.

5
00:00:29,656 --> 00:00:34,908
Reading this is Order Flow. And from today we learn it from zero.

6
00:00:35,908 --> 00:00:39,617
Hello, this is the SPIDER Order Flow series.

7
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:50,830
The series has 24 episodes in 5 parts: basics, volume tools, real Order Flow, big-player footprints, and practical trading.

8
00:00:51,280 --> 00:01:00,031
Today has three questions. What does a candle hide? Why does price move? And what is Order Flow?

9
00:01:00,481 --> 00:01:04,685
No prior knowledge needed. Just watch carefully.

10
00:01:05,686 --> 00:01:11,329
First, how a candle is formed. Say this is five minutes of price.

11
00:01:11,779 --> 00:01:17,735
Price went up, came down, went up again. The whole path is zig-zag.

12
00:01:18,184 --> 00:01:22,704
The candle squeezes this whole path into just four numbers.

13
00:01:23,154 --> 00:01:29,684
Where it started, the highest point, the lowest point, and where it closed.

14
00:01:30,134 --> 00:01:35,202
The whole path in between is gone. That is the candle's biggest weakness.

15
00:01:36,202 --> 00:01:39,755
See the result. These are three different paths.

16
00:01:40,205 --> 00:01:50,654
In the first, price climbed straight up. In the second it fell first, then rallied hard. In the third it went up and tired at the end.

17
00:01:51,104 --> 00:01:54,657
But all three make exactly the same candle.

18
00:01:55,107 --> 00:02:01,454
On the chart you see the same green candle in all three, though the story inside is completely different.

19
00:02:01,904 --> 00:02:06,737
So deciding from the candle alone is deciding on half the information.

20
00:02:07,737 --> 00:02:11,368
Second question. Why does price go up?

21
00:02:11,818 --> 00:02:16,572
Most people say: because there were more buyers. That is wrong.

22
00:02:17,022 --> 00:02:23,631
Every trade has one buyer and one seller. Whatever was bought was exactly what was sold.

23
00:02:24,081 --> 00:02:28,130
So buying and selling are always equal.

24
00:02:28,579 --> 00:02:32,629
So what makes the difference? Urgency.

25
00:02:33,629 --> 00:02:40,864
Think of a vegetable market. A shopkeeper sits with potatoes priced at 20 rupees. He is waiting.

26
00:02:41,315 --> 00:02:46,382
This is the patient trader. In market language, a limit order.

27
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:53,102
Now a customer arrives who needs potatoes right now. He buys at whatever the price is.

28
00:02:53,552 --> 00:02:57,601
This is the aggressive trader. A market order.

29
00:02:58,051 --> 00:03:06,174
If many such urgent customers come, the stock at 20 is gone. The next stock is at 21, then 22.

30
00:03:06,625 --> 00:03:12,738
Price moved up. There were not more buyers; the buyers were just in more of a hurry.

31
00:03:13,188 --> 00:03:19,144
Price is always moved by whoever is in a hurry. This is the foundation of the whole series.

32
00:03:20,144 --> 00:03:22,834
Now the definition of Order Flow is easy.

33
00:03:23,284 --> 00:03:31,799
Order Flow means seeing how much traded at which price, and who was urgent: buyers or sellers.

34
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:39,878
Each level of the candle has two numbers: urgent sellers on one side, urgent buyers on the other.

35
00:03:40,328 --> 00:03:43,489
Reading these numbers is reading Order Flow.

36
00:03:44,489 --> 00:03:47,493
So a candle chart hides three things from us.

37
00:03:47,942 --> 00:03:53,742
One: at which price most trading happened. Where the real fight was.

38
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:59,912
Two: who was aggressive. Were buyers urgent, or sellers.

39
00:04:00,363 --> 00:04:06,894
Three: who is trapped. Who bought or sold at the wrong place and now sits in loss.

40
00:04:07,344 --> 00:04:10,739
All three show up clearly in Order Flow.

41
00:04:11,739 --> 00:04:15,136
Let us see an example. This is the same green candle.

42
00:04:15,585 --> 00:04:20,261
On the chart it looks strong. Most people would think of buying here.

43
00:04:20,711 --> 00:04:27,869
But look inside. At the lower and middle levels buyers were urgent, which is why price rose.

44
00:04:28,319 --> 00:04:36,443
But at the top the picture flipped. Sellers began selling hard there, and the buyers' urgency ran out.

45
00:04:36,893 --> 00:04:41,412
After such a candle, price coming down is one possible scenario.

46
00:04:41,862 --> 00:04:48,132
The candle said buyers won. Order Flow showed sellers had taken over at the top.

47
00:04:49,132 --> 00:04:53,181
One important thing. Order Flow is not magic.

48
00:04:53,631 --> 00:04:58,542
It gives no guarantee. It is not a buy-sell indicator either.

49
00:04:58,992 --> 00:05:05,522
It is just a clearer way to see the market, like clean glasses instead of foggy ones.

50
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:09,838
The decision and the risk management still remain yours.

51
00:05:10,838 --> 00:05:17,369
One more honest point. Spot forex and gold have no single central exchange.

52
00:05:17,819 --> 00:05:24,245
So there is no real volume there, only tick volume: how many times price ticked.

53
00:05:24,695 --> 00:05:30,964
Real Order Flow data comes from the futures market, like gold futures and currency futures.

54
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:36,561
How to use it, we will cover in detail in episode 6.

55
00:05:37,561 --> 00:05:40,800
In this series we will learn five major tools.

56
00:05:41,250 --> 00:05:50,654
Volume Profile, VWAP, Footprint chart, Delta, and Cumulative Delta, or CVD.

57
00:05:51,104 --> 00:05:56,093
Each tool one by one, with animation and examples.

58
00:05:57,093 --> 00:05:58,896
Let us recap today.

59
00:05:59,346 --> 00:06:04,988
One: a candle shows only four numbers and hides the story inside.

60
00:06:05,438 --> 00:06:12,439
Two: buying and selling are always equal. Price is moved by whoever is urgent.

61
00:06:12,889 --> 00:06:19,968
Three: Order Flow is reading how much traded at each price, and who was urgent.

62
00:06:20,968 --> 00:06:26,767
Next episode: how the market really works, like an auction.

63
00:06:27,217 --> 00:06:32,468
